# Test-architecture execution provenance

The TA alias correction changes the tracked semantic-alignment implementation. Current authoring
therefore differs from the frozen94 execution descriptor. The question is whether the existing
forward route produces only that provenance transition, preserves physical/function policy, and
replays as a current empty candidate. Frozen predecessors are immutable. No application database
or shared service configuration is changed; PgAdmin owns disposable databases on18/corpus.

`author.py author <new-output>` acquires a fresh deployed source and clone, checks the candidate,
rehearses it with Alembic Operations inside an outer rollback, and writes reviewed inputs.
`author.py replay <new-output>` checks the subsequently frozen current head and empty candidate.
Author mode is an acquisition-time procedure executed before95 is frozen; it deliberately refuses
an unexpected current head. Replay mode is the current frozen95 check. New output directories
are required; original outputs are retained.

Alembic's standalone MigrationContext/Operations.invoke API was confirmed through Context7 and
the [official runtime API](https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/api/runtime.html) and
[Operations API](https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/ops.html),2026-11-02. Repository native
authoring and authenticated resource ownership retain their existing implementation contracts.

**Passed, bounded Tested,2026-11-02:** authoring and fresh95 replay, including repeated upgrade,
empty candidate and exact native catalog admission after outer rollback. The accepted result is
`ta.native-policy-provenance95` in `records/`; figures belong to that record. The migration changes
only the alignment implementation's descriptor provenance. No application database adoption,
provider result, full95 qualification or performance claim follows. The original failed broad
test receipt and the successful four-case rerun are owned by the TA coordinator.

Initial freeze-utility and evidence-finalization invocation errors were corrected; their logs are
retained in `build/ta-native95-freeze.log` and `build/ta-native95-evidence-finalize.log`. They are
not passing experiments. No predecessor file was overwritten.

